    747:| N/2 universality battery on {f_pi, f_sqfree, f_mu_pos, f_lam_pos, f_sqfree3, PRF} — composition C5 of E1.4 + E2.5 | REFINEMENT | I | Construction succeeded as a *refinement* of E1.4 plus a structural unification of E2.7 + E2.8; does not open polylog. Ran the cheap subset of E1.4's six measures (M1 balanced communication-matrix rank, M2 GF(2) Berlekamp-Massey linear complexity, M3 approximate degree at eps=0.49, M4 PTF degree) on six Boolean functions on {0,...,2^N-1} for N up to 14. Three rank regimes emerge with **closed-form identities**: rank(M_chi_P) = 2^{N/2-1} + 1 exactly (verified N=6,8,10,12,14, the indicator analogue of E2.7's "+2" for the counting function); rank(M_sqfree) = rank(M_mu_pos) = 3·2^{N/2-1} exactly (3/4 of full rank); rank(M_lam_pos) = 2^{N/2} (FULL); rank(M_prf) → 2^{N/2}. Structural cause: rank(M_f) ≤ (1 − rho_f)·2^{N/2} where rho_f is the density of lower-half indices b for which f(a·2^{N/2}+b) = 0 for every row a — for chi_P even-b columns are zero (x even ⇒ x non-prime for x>2), giving rho=1/2; for sqfree, mu_pos the columns with b ≡ 0 mod 4 are zero (4 | x ⇒ not squarefree), giving rho=1/4; for lam_pos no automatic column zeros, giving rho=0. M3 (approximate degree): hits ceil(N/2) exactly for {chi_P, mu_pos, lam_pos} at every tested N, but **deviates** for sqfree (BELOW: 4 vs 5 at N=10), sqfree3 (ABOVE: 4 vs 3 at N=6, 6 vs 5 at N=10), and density-matched PRF (BELOW). M4 PTF mirrors M3. M2 BM/2^N ≈ 0.50 universally across all six functions. **Net new content**: (i) refinement of E1.4 — N/2 universality is a property of the parity-of-Omega family {chi_P, mu_pos, lam_pos}, not of all natural NT Boolean functions; (ii) unification of E2.7 + E2.8 — both rank-deficiency anomalies trace to a common column-zeroing density rho_f; (iii) three exact rank closed forms for non-pi functions. Cites E1.4, E2.5, E2.7, E2.8. See experiments/constructions/n_over_2_universality_class/. | 71 |
