rimality-localised eigenvector with poly-log gap; both Cayley (poly mixing) and coprime/divisor (Ω(1) mixing but no global primality eigenvector) miss the joint condition. Closes ATTACK_VECTORS §D.D4. **Suggested EDGE** (E7.13 candidate): "Szegedy-walk quantisation of any reversible chain on `[1..x]` with adjacency defined by simple arithmetic relation does not yield polylog primality extraction — either spectral gap shrinks polynomially (Cayley class) or eigenvectors capture primality only via degree-class clustering (coprime / divisor class). The two conditions are exhaustive on the families tested." Cites E5.3, E5.8, E7.10, E7.12. Cross-domain reference: Szegedy 2004 (arxiv quant-ph/0401053). See experiments/quantum/szegedy_walk_prime_graphs/. | 80 |
