    18	```
    19	
    20	at every cut `1 ≤ j < d` and every `W ≥ 2`. This is a single-decomposition
    21	statement (MPS / tensor-train).
    22	
    23	E1.9 and E6.3 cover individual additional cases: 2D `φ(x, a)` rank,
    24	DCT / wavelet sparsity. Each was closed in isolation. There is no
    25	family-level closure that says *the entire class of polynomial-bond-dim
    26	tensor-network ansätze fails* on χ_P.
    27	
    28	The leverage: most "what if we use ANSATZ-X" proposals reduce to a single
    29	unfolding-rank check. A clean meta-theorem reducing the entire family to
    30	E2.1 closes dozens of single proposals at once.
